TRADE-OFFS DOCUMENTED
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Pros:
- Prevents single-VM runaway from nuking host
- Per-VM fair share of NVMe
- Real architectural fix
- Built into Proxmox, no external tools

Cons:
- Throttled VMs slower under heavy legitimate IO
- Backup/restore jobs take longer if hit throttle
- Need to balance headroom vs protection

Risks:
- Too low: cluster baseline slow, kubelet probes fail
- Too high: doesn't prevent cascade

Rollback: easy (just remove throttle parameters)

